    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0585" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2407: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d430-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-07T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1919, noon.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 8, 8.38 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>President Hsu sends the Legation following message: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Unless financial assistance [forthcoming] from America or the consortium
                            within a month the Chinese Government will be compelled <pb facs="0586"
                                n="484" xml:id="pg484"/> to make what arrangements it can with Japan
                            in order to escape the consequences of the present financial
                            stringency.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am informed that neither officers nor men of the Army and Navy have been paid
                    for three months. Liu, the Minister of the Navy, has been making short term
                    loans at disastrous rates from different banks, but has been refused further
                    accommodation and so has tendered his resignation to the President two days ago.
                    The resignation has not been accepted, but Liu is absenting himself from Cabinet
                    meetings.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d430-f1" n="53" type="source" xml:id="d430-f1-content">
                <p>Communicated to the Ambassador in Great Britain by telegram No. 5935, Sept. 8, 5
                    p.m., with instructions to repeat to Paris for Marshall and the American
                    Commission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
